comments.body:
Code looks ok. You could try to use helper from `ImageUtils` instead, just to be sure (`dev` branch):

``` javascript
var color = new THREE.Color( 0x0000ff );
var map = THREE.ImageUtils.generateDataTexture( width, height, color );
```

Also your texture is not power-of-2 sized. I didn't try yet DataTexture that wouldn't be power-of-2 sized. DataTextures use directly typed arrays, it's possible there could be some restrictions.
